.TH START-MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-PROXY.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh \- start the reverse tunnel and Caddy for an already running EC2 proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/start\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
The lighter sibling of
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1):
it does not start the EC2 instance or touch DNS. It resolves the instance's
current address (EC2 API, else the public name), then:
.IP \(bu 2
starts the local server with
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1)
unless its health URL already answers (skipped with
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SKIP_SERVER=1 );
.IP \(bu 2
exits 0 at once if the public health URL already answers;
.IP \(bu 2
otherwise runs
.B sudo systemctl start caddy
on the instance (skipped with
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SKIP_REMOTE_CADDY=1 ),
and exits 0 if the public URL now answers;
.IP \(bu 2
otherwise starts the
.B ssh \-N \-R
reverse tunnel under
.BR nohup (1)
unless its pid file is live, and checks the public health URL once.
.SH OPTIONS
None; everything is set by environment variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/mu2edaq-notify-proxy.pem
SSH key (default; forced to mode 600).
.TP
.IR data/mu2edaq-notify-proxy-tunnel.pid ", " data/mu2edaq-notify-proxy-tunnel.log
Tunnel pid and log.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SKIP_SERVER ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SKIP_REMOTE_CADDY ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PUBLIC_URL ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_LOCAL_HEALTH_URL ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_USER ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_KEY ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_REMOTE_BIND ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_LOCAL_TARGET ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_PIDFILE ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_LOGFILE ,
and the shared defaults in
.IR scripts/notify-proxy-common.sh ;
see
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when the public health URL answers. 1 when the instance has no address,
the SSH key is missing, or the tunnel exits immediately; non\-zero from
.B curl
when the final public check fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SKIP_SERVER=1 scripts/start\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh (1),
.BR status-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh (1),
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1),
.BR restore-mu2edaq-notify-tunnel.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group. Part of
